## Data

This example uses the cylinder-wake vorticity snapshots (`VORTALL`)
from `CYLINDER_ALL.mat`. Download `DATA.zip` from the
[book's companion website](https://www.databookuw.com/), extract
`CYLINDER_ALL.mat`, and place it beside the Python script.

**Dataset reference.** S. L. Brunton and J. N. Kutz,
*Data-Driven Science and Engineering: Machine Learning, Dynamical Systems,
and Control*. Cambridge University Press, 2019.
[Book DOI](https://doi.org/10.1017/9781108380690)

## Algorithm reference

J. H. Tu, C. W. Rowley, D. M. Luchtenburg, S. L. Brunton, and J. N. Kutz,
